<article class="env-situation" id="0DLE">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DLE">Situation <span data-tag="0DLE">99.16.3</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to B$ be a morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$. Assume $f$ is proper, flat, and of finite presentation. We denote $\mathcal{C}\! \mathit{omplexes}_{X/B}$ the category whose objects are triples $(T, g, E)$ where </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$T$ is a scheme over $S$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$g : T \to B$ is a morphism over $S$, and setting $X_ T = T \times _{g, B} X$ 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$E$ is an object of $D(\mathcal{O}_{X_ T})$ satisfying conditions (1) and (2) of Lemma <a href="/tag/0DLD" data-tag="0DLD">99.16.2</a>. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> A morphism $(T, g, E) \to (T', g', E')$ is given by a pair $(h, \varphi )$ where </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$h : T \to T'$ is a morphism of schemes over $B$ (i.e., $g' \circ h = g$), and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\varphi : L(h')^*E' \to E$ is an isomorphism of $D(\mathcal{O}_{X_ T})$ where $h' : X_ T \to X_{T'}$ is the base change of $h$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>